; ⚠️ THE GROUND SKINS ARE GONE (the 2026-08-29 geography overhaul). Every road, yard and court in
; this cell used to be a 6 cm BoxMesh slab laid on the floor — forty of them across the realm, and
; they are the literal "flat rectangular floors positioned edge to edge" the overhaul was called to
; remove. The terrain paints them now: WorldTerrainMeshBuilder writes the path mask into vertex
; colour R and the ground-area mask into G, and world_surface.gdshader blends road and activity
; response from those. One authored WorldPathSegmentResource is the road, the shader's colour, the
; terrain's levelling AND the scatter's clearance, instead of a slab that had to agree with three
; other files by hand.
[node name="TarnLanding" type="Node3D"]

[node name="Nav" type="NavigationRegion3D" parent="."]
navigation_mesh = SubResource("NavMesh_tarn")

[node name="NavBaker" type="Node" parent="Nav"]
script = ExtResource("1_navbaker")

